id: CTB-SRC0011-7
source: SRC-0011
section: §7
kind: requirement
extends: LXM-REQ-000199
text: There is one crucial distinction: zero hardcoding does not mean zero executable code or automatically trusting every new technology. A new tool must be discoverable and evaluable, and its compatibility must be verified before use. Production must use a specific, verified resolution for reproducibility and security, while that resolution should be generated and maintained by the governance system rather than duplicated manually.
